-> What is the difference between new/delete and malloc/free?

new/delete are C++ operators that handle object construction and destruction, 
while malloc/free are C functions that only allocate and deallocate raw memory without initialization.

new/delete →
a) C++ operators
b) calls constructor/ destructor
c) new: returns proper type (no casting needed)
d) Failure Handling: new throws exception (bad_alloc)
e) new can initialize memory

malloc/free →
a) C functions
b) do NOT call constructor/destructor
c) malloc: returns void* → needs typecasting
d) Failure Handling: malloc returns NULL
e) malloc does not initialize memeory(garbage value)
